import PolicyPage from "../components/PolicyPage.astro";
---

<PolicyPage
  pageTitle="Refund Policy · Pro Se Fair Play Mediation"
  description="When mediation fees and document preparation fees are refundable, how session credits work, how long a refund takes to appear, and the terms governing both."
  title="Refund"
  titleItalic="policy"
  effective="August 28, 2026"
  version="1.0"
  lede="A refund is for the unforeseeable. By the time two people book mediation they have already agreed to sit down together, so where something gets in the way the aim is to move the session rather than unwind it — but where a refund is right, these are the terms."
>
  <div>
    <h2>The principle</h2>
    <p class="policy-lead">
      Mediation is not a service someone buys on impulse. Both parties have
      already agreed to come to the table before anything is paid for, which is
      why the first response to a problem is almost always a new date rather
      than a refund. Refunds exist for the situations nobody planned for, and
      for the situations where the service was not delivered.
    </p>
    <p>
      Cancellation notice periods, no-shows and rescheduling are on the
      <a class="link-underline" href="/cancellation">Cancellation &amp; Rescheduling Policy</a>
      page. This page covers the money.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2>Mediation sessions</h2>
    <p>
      What is refundable depends on notice. More than twenty-four (24) hours
      before a session, you may take a full refund to the original payment
      method or a full session credit. Inside twenty-four hours, fifty percent
      (50%) of the mediation retainer is retained as a reserved session and
      preparation fee, and the balance may be applied as a one-time credit
      toward a session rescheduled within thirty (30) days. A party who does not
      appear and gives no notice forfeits the full retainer.
    </p>
    <p>
      Two situations produce a full refund regardless of notice: where the
      mediator cancels or withdraws, and where the other party declines to
      proceed at all. Both are set out on the
      <a class="link-underline" href="/cancellation">Cancellation &amp; Rescheduling Policy</a>
      page.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2>Document preparation services</h2>
    <p>
      Parenting Plan Preparation and the Turn-Key Court Packet are flat-fee
      document preparation services and are treated differently from mediation
      sessions.
    </p>
    <h3>Before preparation begins</h3>
    <p>
      Cancel for a full refund at any point before work starts.
    </p>
    <h3>Once preparation has begun</h3>
    <p>
      The fee is non-refundable, as it reflects time already spent. "Begun"
      means the point at which your intake information has been reviewed and
      preparation of your documents has started. Depending on the status of the
      matter and the work completed, a payment may instead be applied as a
      credit toward ongoing or future services.
    </p>
    <h3>Revisions</h3>
    <p>
      The Turn-Key Court Packet includes up to two revisions. Additional
      revisions, or changes requested after the packet has been delivered, are
      quoted separately.
    </p>
    <h3>Third-party costs</h3>
    <p>
      Court filing fees are paid by you directly to the clerk and are not part
      of this fee. Notarization is included where applicable.
    </p>
    <h3>Rejected filings</h3>
    <p>
      These services prepare documents from the information you provide. Because
      the content of your documents is your decision and not the preparer's, a
      filing rejected by the clerk is not itself grounds for a refund. A
      correction of a preparation error made by Pro Se Fair Play Mediation LLC
      is made at no charge.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2>Session credits</h2>
    <p>
      A full session credit issued under these policies is valid for six (6)
      months from the date of issue. A one-time credit following a late
      cancellation must be used for a session scheduled within thirty (30) days,
      subject to availability.
    </p>
    <p>
      Credits are non-transferable, apply only to services provided by Pro Se
      Fair Play Mediation LLC, and have no cash value once elected in place of a
      refund.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2>Payment and refund timing</h2>
    <p>
      Fees are payable in US dollars through the secure payment portal. Refunds
      are issued to the original payment method only. Card refunds typically
      appear within five to ten business days; bank transfer refunds may take
      longer, depending on your financial institution.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2>Questions about a charge</h2>
    <p>
      If you have a question or concern about a charge, please make contact
      directly at
      <a class="link-underline" href="mailto:info@prosefairplaymediation.com">info@prosefairplaymediation.com</a>
      or <a class="link-underline" href="tel:+15619410896">561-941-0896</a>
      before initiating a dispute with your card issuer, so that it can be
      resolved promptly.
    </p>
    <p>
      Any billing discussion is handled without disclosing mediation
      communications, which remain confidential and privileged under section
      44.405, Florida Statutes. A question about an invoice never requires
      either party to reveal what was said in a session.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2>Scope and governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms apply to private, pre-filing mediation and document
      preparation engagements with Pro Se Fair Play Mediation LLC. Court-ordered
      mediation is not offered.
    </p>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Florida, and venue
      for any dispute lies in Palm Beach County, Florida.
    </p>
    <p>
      Emergency situations and unforeseen events are considered on a
      case-by-case basis, with care, at the discretion of Pro Se Fair Play
      Mediation LLC. Nothing on this page is intended to prevent that.
    </p>
  </div>
</PolicyPage>
